# blobly_net project for this demo — open it to watch the two-core capture as a swimlane.
#
# In blobly_net: open this project, Start the channel, then in the Trace Chart (≣) press Record
# to arm capture, Stop to freeze, and Dump to read BOTH cores out in one command (core_mask).
# blobly_net reassembles each per-core ISO-TP block on 0x7E5 (flow control on 0x7E6) and draws
# per-core handler bars, grouped by core. Record/Stop/Dump pause RECORDING, not the cores —
# handlers keep running. The frame ids + both cores' handlers come from the generated manifest
# (gen/trace-manifest.csv, its `# trace frames` rows); blobly_net decodes the fixed protocol
# natively, no DBC. Run this demo first:  make vcan && make run
#
# Paths are relative to blobly_net's working dir (it resolves the manifest from where it is
# launched, not from this file). Launch blobly_net from this directory, or use the ready-to-open
# copy at blobly_net/projects/trace-multicore.blobnet. The swimlane renders either way — handler
# names resolve when the manifest is found, else lanes read "handler N".
project:
  name: trace-multicore
  version: 2

buses:
  - name: CAN1
    adapter: vcan
    address: vcan0
    protocol: can
    bitrate: 500000
    mode: monitor
    enabled: true
    manifest: gen/trace-manifest.csv
